# Case G: Seated Meals

## Client
- **Mr. Gibbs**, Associate Head of School, Pomfret School. He runs the school's seated meals (formal dinners at assigned round tables, with student waiters).

## Team
- Christoph Ortenburg (lead developer), Abdul Hakim Al Khamisi, Lexi Godwin and Logan Lee.
- Cayden Auyang (president) leads the client meetings. Luke Ryan (vice president).

## Status
- Building the first version for Candlelight, Dec 15, 2026. Mr. Gibbs gets the lists to review by Dec 8, 2026.
- The full spec is `docs/spec.md`. Calls made while building are in `docs/decisions.md`; where the two differ, `docs/decisions.md` wins. Never rewrite `docs/spec.md`.

## What the tool is
- A Google Sheets tool (Apps Script, plain JavaScript): it seats the attending faculty (with households and guests), seats every attending student by rules Mr. Gibbs turns on and ranks, picks each table's waiter and assistant fairly across the year, checks every rule and writes the tabs he shares.
- A plain program: no AI, no model calls, no network, no new dependencies. Same input and same Seed, same output.
- Shared logic is in `core/`, the Sheets side is `apps-script/Main.gs`, and `paste-into-apps-script/SeatedMeals.gs` is generated by `npm run bundle`. Tests run with `npm test` against a fake spreadsheet.

## Safety rules (they don't bend)
- The repo is public. Build and test with made-up people only. Never put a real student's or faculty member's name, email, table or any other detail in code, tests, fixtures, docs, commit messages or PR text. Club members' names as the team are fine. Practice emails end in @example.org.
- Nobody working on the code sees the real data. The real run happens in Google Sheets, in the school's Google account, by a person.
- The program never writes to the tabs people fill in (Students, Faculty, Faculty list, Past event). Only Make practice data writes those, and only into a spreadsheet whose Students and Faculty tabs are empty.
- The shared tabs (SM By first name, SM By form, SM By table, SM Faculty) show only names, form, table, role and guests. Never gender, boarding or day, dorm, advisory, sport, email or rule details.
- No sheet links, spreadsheet IDs or school email addresses anywhere in the repo.
- Don't merge, don't push to main, and don't edit `.github/CODEOWNERS`.
- Add a `.env.example` the moment any credential or ID is needed. None is needed today.

